riant of this problem where we additionally require the graphs to have large minimum degree. Both of these problems turn out be intimately related to two other problems regarding maximally independent sets of a given size in $K_3$K 3​-free graphs and generalisations of these problems to $K_r$K r​ with $r \\geq 4$r≥4. The first problem is to maximise the number of maximally independent sets given the number of vertices and the second problem is to minimise the number of edges given the number of maximally independent sets. They are interesting in their own right.\n\nView PaperPDF\n\n## BibTeX\n\nCopy\n\n@misc{calbet2024twinfreekrsaturatedgraphsmaximally, title={Twin-free $K_r$-saturated Graphs and Maximally Independent Sets in $K_3$-free Graphs}, author={Asier Calbet}, year={2024}, eprint={2411.19267}, archivePrefix={arXiv}, primaryClass={math.CO}, url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.19267}, }--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAsymptotic saturation conjecture for the convex geometric hypergraph S_3 | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/352008/asymptotic-saturation-conjecture-for-the-convex-geometric-hy)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Asymptotic saturation conjecture for the convex geometric hypergraph $S_3$S 3​ ... The paper determines the order of magnitude of the saturation number for every two-edge convex geometric $3$3-uniform hypergraph except $S_3$S 3​; the displayed estimate is presented as the authors' best guess and remains open. ... Jason O'Neill and Sam Spiro, “Saturation Problems in Convex Geometric Hypergraphs”, arXiv:2109.09931 (2021).\n\nAsymptotic saturation conjecture for the convex geometric hypergraph $S_3$S 3​\n\nLet $S_3$S 3​ be the two-edge convex geometric $3$3-uniform hypergraph denoted by $S_3$S 3​ in the source, and let $\\operatorname{sat}_\\circlearrowright(n,S_3)$sat↻​(n,S 3​) denote its saturation number on $n$n vertices. Saturation conjecture for $S_3$S 3​.\n\n$$\\operatorn